-- Row il-77. THE REFERENCES, as typed values: the instruments, the places, the instructions and printed texts the two items read, item I1 and item I2, and the commencements as the pages print them.
-- Tests of the controls are in pr77-tests-controls.l4, tests that pin the readings are in pr77-tests-readings.l4, and the assertions that FAIL on purpose (two, one per item) are in pr77-tests-red.l4.
--
-- THE QUOTATION LINES.
-- `src:N` lines are expanded mechanically from the excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation (UNOFFICIAL, so CONSOLIDATION-ONLY) by tools/srcquote.py; N is the line number in the whole page, which the excerpt's header lists.
-- `ext:[tag]` lines quote the Hebrew printed on a deposited image of an official instrument (registers/source-bundle/pages/); the tag names the instrument and the printed page. They are official instruments.
-- Every Hebrew string typed below is a stretch of the ext: line above it, and tools/hebcheck.py checks that each Hebrew run of this module is in the excerpt or on an ext: line.
-- Where a quotation mark is printed around a term, the ext: line types it as the Hebrew gershayim.
-- Nothing is quoted from memory. Every date, number and section below is on a quotation line or in NOTES.md.

§ `References`

